# Accepted trivy findings for deploy/aws/tofu, each with its reason.
# Run: trivy config --ignorefile deploy/aws/tofu/.trivyignore deploy/aws/tofu

# ECR "tags are mutable": the repos are IMMUTABLE_WITH_EXCLUSION, immutable
# except buildcache*, which the registry build cache must rewrite. trivy does
# not model the exclusion mode.
AVD-AWS-0031
# ECR / EBS / site bucket not on a customer-managed key: encrypted with the
# AWS-managed key. Nothing outside the account reads them, so a CMK adds
# $1/month each and no access boundary (secrets and logs DO use CMKs).
AVD-AWS-0033
AVD-AWS-0027
AVD-AWS-0132
# Unrestricted egress: the NAT instance (forwarding to the internet is its
# job) and 443/80 out from tasks and the monitor box, which call Google,
# Anthropic, APNs, Resend, WorkOS, Slack and AWS APIs by hostname.
AVD-AWS-0104
# Public load balancer: it is the front door.
AVD-AWS-0053
# WAF: out of scope for this wave (DESIGN.md).
AVD-AWS-0011
# Access logging on buckets / CloudFront, VPC flow logs, CloudTrail to
# CloudWatch, container insights, RDS performance insights: cost, and in the
# access-log cases a store of client IPs we otherwise do not keep. CloudTrail
# to S3 is on. ALB access logs are a variable (alb_access_logs).
AVD-AWS-0089
AVD-AWS-0010
AVD-AWS-0178
AVD-AWS-0162
AVD-AWS-0034
AVD-AWS-0133
# RDS IAM auth: the control store authenticates with a password in its
# Secrets Manager DATABASE_URL; IAM tokens would need a code change.
AVD-AWS-0176
